{
 "slug": "html_lists_unordered",
 "course": "html",
 "order": 34,
 "url": "/html/html_lists_unordered.asp",
 "title": "HTML Unordered Lists",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "h1",
   "text": "HTML Unordered Lists"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The HTML <ul> tag defines an unordered\n(bulleted) list."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Unordered HTML List"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "An unordered list starts with the <ul> tag. Each list item starts with the\n<li> tag."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The list items will be marked with bullets (small black circles) by default:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ul>\n\n<li>Coffee</li>\n  <li>Tea</li>\n\n<li>Milk</li>\n\n</ul>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_unordered2"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Unordered HTML List - Choose List Item Marker"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The CSS list-style-type property is used to define the style of the\nlist item marker. It can have one of the following values:"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Value",
    "Description"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "disc",
     "Sets the list item marker to a bullet (default)"
    ],
    [
     "circle",
     "Sets the list item marker to a circle"
    ],
    [
     "square",
     "Sets the list item marker to a square"
    ],
    [
     "none",
     "The list items will not be marked"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Disc"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ul style=\"list-style-type:disc;\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n\n  <li>Tea</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ul>",
   "caption": "Example - Disc"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_unordered_disc"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Circle"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle;\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n\n  <li>Tea</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ul>",
   "caption": "Example - Circle"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_unordered_circle"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "Square"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ul style=\"list-style-type:square;\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n\n  <li>Tea</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ul>",
   "caption": "Example - Square"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_unordered_square"
  },
  {
   "type": "h3",
   "text": "No List Marker"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ul style=\"list-style-type:none;\">\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n\n  <li>Tea</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ul>",
   "caption": "Example - None"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_unordered_none"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Nested HTML Lists"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Lists can be nested (list inside list):"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<ul>\n  <li>Coffee</li>\n  <li>Tea\n\n    <ul>\n\n<li>Black tea</li>\n      <li>Green tea</li>\n\n    </ul>\n\n</li>\n  <li>Milk</li>\n</ul>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_nested"
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "variant": "note",
   "text": "A list item (<li>) can contain\n  a new list, and other HTML elements, like images and links, etc."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Horizontal List with CSS"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "HTML lists can be styled in many different ways with CSS."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "One popular way is to style a list horizontally, to create a navigation menu:"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "html",
   "text": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<style>\nul {\n  list-style-type: none;\n\n    margin: 0;\n  padding: 0;\n  overflow: hidden;\n  background-color: #333333;\n}\n\nli {\n  float: left;\n}\n\nli a {\n  display: block;\n  color: white;\n  text-align: center;\n  padding: 16px;\n  text-decoration: none;\n}\n\nli a:hover {\n  background-color: #111111;\n}\n\n </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><a href=\"#home\">Home</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#news\">News</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#about\">About</a></li>\n\n </ul>\n\n</body>\n</html>",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryhtml_lists_menu"
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
   "variant": "note",
   "text": "You can learn much more about CSS in our CSS Tutorial."
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "Chapter Summary"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "ordered": false,
   "items": [
    "Use the HTML <ul> element to define an unordered list",
    "Use the CSS list-style-type property to define the list item marker",
    "Use the HTML <li> element to define a list item",
    "Lists can be nested",
    "List items can contain other HTML elements",
    "Use the CSS property float:left to display a list horizontally"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "HTML List Tags"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "headers": [
    "Tag",
    "Description"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "<ul>",
     "Defines an unordered list"
    ],
    [
     "<ol>",
     "Defines an ordered list"
    ],
    [
     "<li>",
     "Defines a list item"
    ],
    [
     "<dl>",
     "Defines a description list"
    ],
    [
     "<dt>",
     "Defines a term in a description list"
    ],
    [
     "<dd>",
     "Describes the term in a description list"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "note",
